{"chapter": "descent", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "023F", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:8815bbe2501b734bd3185ef1a5a33e88eb4e515294415d7408bf15c190e0d684", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nHere is how the complex relates to the question of effectivity.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:cc45ed74c2bf5afaff71a2b1f41c18849ca9cd9c0a67b3336082d5678274cf3a", "unit_id": "tag:023F:prose-0005"}
{"chapter": "descent", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "023F", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$R \\to A$", "MATH_0002": "$(N, \\varphi)$", "MATH_0003": "$(N, \\varphi)$", "MATH_0004": "$$\nA \\otimes_R H^0(s(N_\\bullet)) \\longrightarrow N\n$$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-recognize-effective}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:d4c527cd6c095554d345e514914e6846abf0267168367d11f53293508a0732cd", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:e80fb503cb93c6b8e6ced7502ba2745bdaac3c2f1e73e00963622ccb70dc3aa0", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a faithfully flat ring map.\nLet <MATH_0002> be a descent datum.\nThen <MATH_0003> is effective if and only if the canonical\nmap\n<MATH_0004>\nis an isomorphism.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:86966c7acd02988cf38e2d1436d6e7d6a8fdf74db9392bc5a984b23e9bd4ff59", "unit_id": "tag:039W:statement"}
{"chapter": "descent", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "023F", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$(N, \\varphi)$", "MATH_0002": "$N = A \\otimes_R M$", "MATH_0003": "$\\varphi = can$", "MATH_0004": "$H^0(s(N_\\bullet)) = M$", "MATH_0005": "$M = H^0(s(N_\\bullet))$", "MATH_0006": "$R$", "MATH_0007": "$N$", "MATH_0008": "$M = \\{n \\in N \\mid 1 \\otimes n = \\varphi(n \\otimes 1)\\}$", "MATH_0009": "$A \\otimes_R M \\to N$", "MATH_0010": "$\\varphi$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-canonical-descent-datum-cosimplicial}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-ff-exact}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:5387a832b232548250ec0be65ed8c23910430902daf233ea73d765e40e311705", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:2aeb0302b437eb484c69b0b8ad5ec290c684b7c6274df907d5fafe9d209491e9", "source_text": "If <MATH_0001> is effective, then we may write <MATH_0002>\nwith <MATH_0003>. It follows that <MATH_0004> by\nLemmas <REF_0001>\nand <REF_0002>. Conversely, suppose the map of the lemma\nis an isomorphism. In this case set <MATH_0005>.\nThis is an <MATH_0006>-submodule of <MATH_0007>,\nnamely <MATH_0008>.\nThe only thing to check is that via the isomorphism\n<MATH_0009>\nthe canonical descent data agrees with <MATH_0010>.\nWe omit the verification.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:9081ee390c2075dca79d661967c658af403a0f76b0c8f296b1eaebb542d2dbd3", "unit_id": "tag:039W:proof"}
{"chapter": "descent", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "023F", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$R \\to A$", "MATH_0002": "$R \\to R'$", "MATH_0003": "$A' = R' \\otimes_R A$", "MATH_0004": "$R' \\to A'$", "MATH_0005": "$R \\to A$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-descent-descends}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:69c8241a8e2adb429d3ecb02934929da3ab8f227424854450ceb9b54263211f8", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:babf9932aad78e825fd5f5494106697310ffc54bb7bea895a9890457324128e6", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a faithfully flat ring map, and let <MATH_0002>\nbe faithfully flat. Set <MATH_0003>. If all descent data\nfor <MATH_0004> are effective, then so are all descent data for <MATH_0005>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:5ca479eb5c2c9b3b2305dc9367263b88f823af564bfa98df15c08a5bb86fcb68", "unit_id": "tag:039X:statement"}
{"chapter": "descent", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "023F", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$(N, \\varphi)$", "MATH_0002": "$R \\to A$", "MATH_0003": "$N' = R' \\otimes_R N = A' \\otimes_A N$", "MATH_0004": "$\\varphi' = \\text{id}_{R'} \\otimes \\varphi$", "MATH_0005": "$\\varphi$", "MATH_0006": "$(N', \\varphi')$", "MATH_0007": "$R' \\to A'$", "MATH_0008": "$H^0(s(N'_\\bullet)) = R' \\otimes_R H^0(s(N_\\bullet))$", "MATH_0009": "$A' \\otimes_{R'} H^0(s(N'_\\bullet)) \\to N'$", "MATH_0010": "$A$", "MATH_0011": "$A \\otimes_R H^0(s(N)) \\to N$", "MATH_0012": "$A \\to A'$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-recognize-effective}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:2122b6543b27c076ad8fd427db0b88e76dd717b6eacf821980051bb2ba747beb", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:652bf651e3d14a35e58abb599a313b78c7faf3361c98dbf2b713d50ebaa66ce5", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a descent datum for <MATH_0002>.\nSet <MATH_0003>, and denote\n<MATH_0004> the base change\nof the descent datum <MATH_0005>. Then <MATH_0006> is\na descent datum for <MATH_0007> and\n<MATH_0008>.\nMoreover, the map\n<MATH_0009> is identified\nwith the base change of the <MATH_0010>-module map\n<MATH_0011> via the faithfully flat map\n<MATH_0012>. Hence we conclude by Lemma <REF_0001>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:d9d8109ab9c098ef4743c49e380930f2cbc047d227be31ba5e95574f5847cb7e", "unit_id": "tag:039X:proof"}
{"chapter": "descent", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "023F", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{remark-homotopy-equivalent-cosimplicial-algebras}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:518e17b3408d979087e670220aa8fa8f490f25b444c1fe1b977f611fa090146e", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nHere is the main result of this section.\nIts proof may seem a little clumsy; for a more highbrow approach see\nRemark <REF_0001> below.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:aba9eb28f418f4630a15e35ce2366f70170a3510c733fc63fe7314122490359a", "unit_id": "tag:023F:prose-0006"}
